P8-conformance-001 integrator patch (outside the unit's write scope: gates/phase-8.toml, interfaces/README.md).

Rationale. conformance-full --config-pin refuses a golden subject's report unless this run's passing gate logs carry
`CONFORMANCE-BOOT: <subject> artifact <A> config <H>` with A = the judged artifact_sha256 and H = the pin in
conformance/config-pin.toml; no Phase-8 gate prints that line yet, so without this patch conformance-full is red for
both golden subjects by design (no boot evidence). The patch appends conformance/boot-pin (which boots the artifact
with its golden config and requires check-config, the boot log line of the started pid and /healthz to agree) to the
two gates that already produce the judged artifacts: release-verify (floor, on kamrui; artifact
target/release-out/artifacts/aegis-floor) and release-rebuild (cmvp, laptop; the A-side copy
target/release-rebuild/cmvp/A/aegis-cmvp). Both gates run before conformance-full, so their logs are in the window
the runner accepts. Two follow-ups are needed after applying: (1) the cmvp pin in conformance/config-pin.toml is empty
(a FIPS-CMVP listener only loads in the cmvp build, which this unit did not build); copy the hash from the first
release-rebuild log's CONFORMANCE-BOOT line into it after checking the line, in the same change that records the
check; (2) if either release artifact does not run on the host that boots it (container-built binary vs host libc),
move the boot-pin call to a gate on a host that can run it; the artifact sha in the record must still equal the
release digest. The README row records the F13 additive members (README is not a frozen file; F13 itself is
re-frozen in the unit's commit). Changing a gate's cmd changes its logged `$ cmd` line; conformance/run reads the cmd
from the same toml, so nothing else moves.

--- a/gates/phase-8.toml
+++ b/gates/phase-8.toml
@@ -558,14 +558,14 @@
 
 [[gate]]
 name = "release-verify"
-cmd = "ci/release/pipeline.sh --profile floor --out target/release-out && ci/release/verify.py --allow-test-keys target/release-out"
+cmd = "ci/release/pipeline.sh --profile floor --out target/release-out && ci/release/verify.py --allow-test-keys target/release-out && python3 -I conformance/boot-pin --subject aegis-bin-floor --binary target/release-out/artifacts/aegis-floor"
 selftest = "ci/release/verify.py --self-test"
 heavy = true
 remote = "kamrui"
 
 [[gate]]
 name = "release-rebuild"
-cmd = "ci/release/rebuild.sh --a kamrui --b quiet --profiles floor,cmvp"
+cmd = "ci/release/rebuild.sh --a kamrui --b quiet --profiles floor,cmvp && python3 -I conformance/boot-pin --subject aegis-bin-cmvp --binary target/release-rebuild/cmvp/A/aegis-cmvp"
 selftest = "ci/release/rebuild.sh --self-test"
 heavy = true
 
